--- !u!114 &1956148946
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1956148943}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "She builds this Her Memories moment as an almost-still scene: the heroine
    is singing, and light falls from above like an afternoon that never ends. Her
    body is arranged like a sculpture, like a stone figure\u2014beautiful, composed,
    watched, frozen\u2014as if staying here means never having to face what is outside.
    The whole space is a shimmering mirage, bright and soft, held together by an
    illusion that is carefully maintained.\n\nBut what she wants to express is the
    danger inside that beauty. The more sunlit it looks, the more it resembles a
    cover for inner rot. She frames the scene\u2019s underlying atmosphere as a ruined
    ancestral shrine\u2014its exterior still carries a solemn shape, but inside it
    is damp, hollow, and decaying. The singing is not only romantic here; it becomes
    a kind of sustained self-hypnosis, making someone believe everything is still
    intact, when in fact it has been collapsing from within all along."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: fb31704cec070074ca40032b135cceca, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -2758856410231806141, guid: fb31704cec070074ca40032b135cceca, type: 2}
